# IES -> BFO mapping axioms (subject = IES class). Project 3, steps 4 and 8.
# Review notes for every candidate row are in mapping-decisions.md.
#
# Design stance: IES is a 4D (BORO) ontology in which every Entity is also a State of
# itself (e.g. ies:Person is a subclass of both ies:Entity and ies:PersonState). Mapping
# ies:State to BFO occurrent while mapping ies:Person to BFO object makes ies:Person
# unsatisfiable, so no continuant-side IES classes are mapped here. The mappings below sit
# on the occurrent side, where IES's spatio-temporal extents and BFO's occurrents agree.

@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix obo:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/> .
@prefix ies:  <http://ies.data.gov.uk/ontology/ies4#> .

<http://example.org/ontology-tradecraft/project-3/ies-mapping> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:comment "IES-to-BFO alignment axioms whose subject is an IES class." .

# Converse of bfo-mapping.ttl; together they entail ies:ParticularPeriod = BFO temporal interval.
ies:ParticularPeriod rdfs:subClassOf obo:BFO_0000202 .   # temporal interval

# IES PeriodOfTime: "an Element whose spatial extent is everywhere, but whose temporal
# extent is limited" = a stretch of time. Every such period is a BFO temporal region
# ("an occurrent over which processes can unfold"). Only subClassOf: BFO temporal regions
# also include zero-dimensional instants, which are not IES periods.
ies:PeriodOfTime rdfs:subClassOf obo:BFO_0000008 .       # temporal region

# IES Event: "an activity or incident, involving one or more participating entities"
# BFO process: "an occurrent that has some temporal proper part and ... has some material
# entity as participant". Every IES event is a BFO process; the converse does not hold
# (IES reserves Event for activities and incidents of interest, not every process).
# The structural pass did not pair these (process also carries 'only' axioms), so this
# came out of the definition review.
ies:Event rdfs:subClassOf obo:BFO_0000015 .              # process
